SUMMARY:Götterdämmerung - Royal Ballet & Opera 26-27 Season @ WTW Newquay
DESCRIPTION:Götterdämmerung - Royal Ballet & Opera 26-27 Season (5h 50min)\
 n\nAn earth in ruin. The twilight of the Gods. \nDeception leads to treac
 hery\, then devastation\, when Siegfried is tricked into betraying Brünnhi
 lde. Learning the truth of her beloved's innocence\, Brünnhilde at last re
 turns the ring to the Rhinemaidens\, before ordering that Valhalla be swal
 lowed in flames. For the long-awaited finale of Wagner's epic saga\, direc
 tor Barrie Kosky situates the rich apocalyptic drama in a contemporary wor
 ld of dream-like turmoil. Antonio Pappano\, Conductor Laureate of The Roya
 l Opera\, returns to take on the impassioned\, otherworldly music – includ
 ing Siegfried's transporting Funeral March and Brünnhilde's electrifying I
 mmolation Scene. The brilliant cast is led by Elisabet Strid\, Andreas Sch
 ager and Mika Kares\, who together with the full forces of the Orchestra o
 f the Royal Opera House and the Royal Opera Chorus bring opera's greatest 
 journey to its shattering end.\n\nFilm release at WTW Cinemas Newquay\nBoo
 k tickets: https://wtwcinemas.co.uk/newquay/film/5560/gtterdmmerung-royal-
 ballet-opera-2627-season\n\nFilm details: https://evenwebb.github.io/wtw-c
 inemas/films/g-tterd-mmerung-royal-ballet-opera-26-27-season.html
LOCATION:WTW Cinemas Newquay
